</span></span><span>              ## Observer Pattern Fundamentals
</span><span>             =20
</span><span>              ### What is Observer Pattern?
</span><span>              The Observer Pattern defines one-to-many depende=
ncy between objects where
</span><span>              when one object changes state, all dependents ar=
e notified automatically.
</span><span>             =20
</span><span>              ### Real-world Analogies:
</span><span>              1. **Newsletter Subscription**: Publisher sends =
newsletter to all subscribers
</span><span>              2. **Social Media**: Influencer posts, all follo=
wers get notified
</span><span>              3. **Stock Market**: Price changes notify all in=
terested traders
</span><span>             =20
</span><span>              ### Core Components:
</span><span>              - **Subject (Observable)**: The object being wat=
ched
</span><span>              - **Observer**: Objects that want to be notified
</span><span>              - **Subscribe/Unsubscribe**: Mechanism to add/re=
move observers
</span><span>              - **Notify**: Mechanism to inform all observers
